\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces One shared dolphin cycle and an illustrative recorded encounter. Continuous near-prey pressure for H is followed by a feasible strike preferring fewer prey neighbours and ordinary recovery. Bird presence does not change this dolphin rule. Top and side views show original development school 39061002 at 12T; paths and captures cover 6--12T. The snapshot was fixed before the sweep and does not certify compactness, completed herding or a causal mechanism.\relax }}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Distinct cohorts under the same dolphin rule. Colour identifies school within each two-school panel; circles/squares identify capture-stream settings 61001/61002. Lines join dolphin-only and mixed outcomes. The development totals 41\ensuremath  {\rightarrow }48 and follow-up 87\ensuremath  {\rightarrow }101 involve four distinct pilot school geometries overall; the two follow-up settings do not add independent schools. Separate panels show the same eight later schools across coarse/fine 36T grids, with mean diamonds and 97.5\% marginal bootstrap intervals only for the coarse primary means. The fine check did not rerun the earlier positive cohorts.\relax }}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Complete declared H\ensuremath  {\times }G response map on four previously observed schools. Mean paired changes and pointwise 95\% whole-school bootstrap intervals are shown per predator over the full 36T encounter. Comparators are same-H D-only, same-count G-only and the best-tested D-only H chosen across this discovery bank and reselected within each draw. All nine mixed settings and signs are retained; all 36 school contrasts and absolute returns are in the notebook. Panels use separate symmetric colour ranges. Selected large cells are exploratory discoveries, not confirmed optima.\relax }}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Descriptive response across every dolphin-bearing H\ensuremath  {\times }G setting, including G=0. Faint points show all four schools and lines show equal-school means. Live-fish r90 and outward fraction are time-averaged over observed nonempty saved frames without selected post-dive windows. Eligible contacts and captures use the full 36T denominator. Prey removal and survivor selection can change fish-state summaries; these associations do not establish causal mediation, completed herding or biological cooperation.\relax }}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
